  "marked": false,
  "answer": "<p>The command that should be included in the <b>pre_build</b> stage is to get the Docker login credentials for Amazon ECR, which is accomplished with the AWS CLI command to fetch a temporary authentication token (<b>Obtain an authentication token for Docker to interact with ECR using the AWS CLI.</b>). This is essential because ECR requires authentication before you can push images to it. Skipping this step will cause the push operation to fail due to lack of permission.<br><br>Let's break down the other options:<br><br><i>\"Initiate the Docker image build and tag with the specified ECR URI.\"</i> is incorrectly placed in the pre_build and actually belongs to the build phase, as image building is performed there.<br><br><i>\"Push the created image to the specified ECR repository.\"</i> should be part of the post_build phase as the image must be built and tagged before it can be pushed.<br><br><i>\"Tag the Docker image using the ECR repository URI.\"</i> is typically performed just after building the image, making it appropriate for the build or pre_post_build phase but not pre_build, as you can't tag an image before it exists.<br><br><b>Tip:</b> Always ensure you authenticate to ECR in pre_build to allow docker commands to work against your ECR repository throughout the build process.</p>",
  "query": "<p>An AWS DevOps engineer uses CodePipeline to automate building a Docker image and pushing it to Amazon ECR. The source code is hosted in CodeCommit, and the image build and push actions occur in CodeBuild. The buildspec.yml has three phases: pre_build, build, and post_build. In this context, which command belongs in the <b>pre_build</b> phase to enable the Docker push to ECR?</p>",
